  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "The sum of two numbers is \\(S.\\) Suppose \\(3\\) is added to each number and then each of the resulting numbers is doubled. What is the sum of the final two numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2S + 3\\)",
    "B": "\\(3S + 2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3S + 6\\)",
    "D": "\\(2S + 6\\)",
    "E": "\\(2S + 12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Adding \\(3\\) to each of two numbers increases their total by \\(3+3=6\\), so the new sum is \\(S+6\\). Doubling both numbers doubles their total. Therefore the final sum is\n\\[\n2(S+6)=\\boxed{2S+12},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{E}\\).",
